diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..4bc5552 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,72 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Receiving events
+
+Whenever something happens on a board, Fizzy delivers it to every active webhook on
+that board that is subscribed to the event's action. Every event is delivered exactly
+once: we don't retry, so a slow or broken receiver is never bothered about the same
+event twice.
+
+__Request:__
+
+```
+POST https://api.example.com/webhooks
+User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook
+Content-Type: application/json
+X-Webhook-Timestamp: 2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z
+X-Webhook-Signature: 5257a869e7ecebeda32affa62cdca3fa51cad7e77a0e56ff536d0ce8e108d8bd
+```
+
+The body is the delivered event as JSON:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": { "...": "..." },
+  "board": { "...": "..." },
+  "creator": { "...": "..." }
+}
+```
+
+Receivers that expect a chat message (Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp Campfire) get a
+short message about the event instead of the whole event. The message is sent as
+`text` for Slack, as `message` for Campfire, and as `content` for Basecamp Campfire.
+
+__Verifying the signature:__
+
+The `X-Webhook-Signature` header holds the `HMAC` `SHA256` of the request body,
+computed with the webhook's `signing_secret`, so you can verify that the request came
+from us:
+
+```ruby
+OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest("SHA256", signing_secret, request_body)
+```
+
+## Delivery log
+
+Every delivery attempt is logged, so you can see how it went. A delivery is either
+`pending`, `in_progress`, `completed`, or `errored`, and holds the request headers we
+sent and the response we got back.
+
+__Response:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdn",
+  "state": "completed",
+  "request": { "headers": { "..." : "..." } },
+  "response": { "code": 200, "error": null }
+}
+```
+
+The log keeps a week of deliveries. After that, they are cleaned up.
+
+## Switching off a misbehaving receiver
+
+A receiver that keeps failing gets switched off automatically: after ten deliveries
+in a row that failed, all of them within an hour, the webhook is deactivated and
+stops receiving events. Reactivating it gives it a fresh start.
